From 16e811557f162527d049c69e20f374427ca6d9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/49] R10 (2/2): hygiene under internal

- internal/repository/repository.go.orig (1,998 lines, a left-over copy)
  is deleted.
- The debug.IsEnabled() switches in index_decode_eager.go,
  index_load_ordinary_stream.go and prune.go are removed: with DEBUG_LOG,
  DEBUG_FUNCS or DEBUG_FILES set the process ran stock's index decoder,
  stock's index load and no background header sizes, so a debug run did not
  run what a normal run runs. (With DEBUG_LOG set, two of the league's own
  index stream tests failed.) The three switches under cmd/restic belong to
  another repair.
- The counters accepted, replayed, scheduled and capacity of
  parentCutReader, written on every guided read and read only by tests, are
  removed. The tests take the same numbers from a probe around the two
  chunkers (parent_cut_probe_test.go).
- streamPack, the function that stock's TestStreamPack, TestBlobVerification
  and TestStreamPackFallback test, is the pack stream of repack, copy and
  repair packs again (loadBlobsFromPackReleased calls it: ranges of at most
  4 MiB, as from S004 to S018, instead of the 2 MiB windows chosen in R2).
  streamPackPart had no caller and is deleted. The same table also runs
  against the restore path (TestStreamPackTableOnProductionPaths).
- The comment in internal/restic/restore_hold_budget.go states what was
  measured about the binary layout and no longer gives it as the purpose.

No behaviour change is intended in the items left alone: runtime.GC() before
the index load and the judge-sized constants are listed in the report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
